A||||12||Indy-2M4||Fiero Daily Driver....or not??||||1||
Z||000000||Indy-2M4||11-20-2001||06:01 AM||||I don't know if I am being anal retentive or what, but until a week ago, I was gonna save the '84 SE for the "only on nice days and weekends" car. But now that I have the Indy for "Special Occasions", I am driving the SE more. It only has 102,000miles on it, clean and was one of the earlier production cars (#20,000 and something out of 186,000 made for that year). Should I continue to driver her almost dailey or keep her only for weekends, etc. I just love driving them so much. Wonder if I should find a ragged one to beat around. Cant afford any more room for cars....HELP!<P>------------------<BR><BR>F.K.A. KathyHL<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://sofa.iwarp.com/IndyFiero2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||11-20-2001||10:09 AM||||It really depends on how you feel about it.  If you really like driving it and don't mind putting the wear and tear on it then you might as well keep driving it.  Also, if you don't like to have three cars sitting around, and pay the associated costs (both insurance/registration and maintenance) on three cars you might want to keep driving it.<P>Just because its an 84 SE wouldn't stop me from driving it.  I mean no offense to your car, but of the two your Indy is a LOT more collectable than the SE. <P>I'd say keep your money, keep drivng the SE and enjoy it.  In the future if you wear something out (even the engine) you can always replace it or get yourself a new Fiero!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||11-20-2001||10:29 AM||||I'd say drive it and keep the indy for the weekends.<P>I see the fiero as more of a fun car then a collectable car.  But I dont drive mine daily. (only summer weekends)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Springtyme||11-20-2001||10:38 AM||||My 88 had 72,000 miles on it when I first got it (now it has 74,some hehehe). I wasn't gonna drive it much, just to work and the store and such, but its such a fun car I just can't do it! I say do what you want, don't feel bad about putting miles on it, you can always rebuild another engine and swap it once the miles get too high  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||11-20-2001||10:54 AM||||I know how you feel. The 88coupeV6 only goes to shows and some weekend drives, but the 88 Yellow GT gets driven 100miles daily. I keep it up but how good is it to keep adding miles? It is up to 170,000 now and only had 160,000 on it when I got it this summer.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It is a lot of fun to drive but rare as only 241 yellow GT's were made. It runs like new as I take great care of my cars.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000005||Indy-2M4||11-22-2001||08:42 AM||||Thanks for advice, guys. I think as long as there is not any snow/ice on the roads, I'm gonna keep driving the SE. They are such addictive little cars. My dailey driver is a 95 Neon coupe tricked out. It is a lot of fun too, but not as much fun as a Fiero! Thanks again and enjoy your cars.<BR>Kathy||||reg||1
